  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased satisfaction of customers of RGZ services</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2004-04-01" value="62%" year="2004">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">62% of respondants of the 2004 survey state that fees are not too high and services are satisfactory.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2004-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2012-02-29"></period-end>
     <target value="25% increase on the baseline figure.">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Services are dramatically improved and customers are generally satisfied.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="8% increase on the base line figure.">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The final survey was completed in May 2011. There is 85% of people who are aware of the RGA services on property registrationcompared to 60% in 2008.  There is an increased level of positive reputation of RGA in the society from 66% in 2008 to 78% in 2011.And finally there is 67% of people who assess the quality of RGA services as good, very good, or excellent. Only 13% consider theservices unsatisfactory. The base line survey did not have a category for &apos;neither satisfied nor dissatisfied&apos;, and it could beargued that87% equates to the figures in 2004, representing a 35% increase on the base rate.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase in numbers of mortgages as a percentage of the total number of transactions</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2005-12-30" value="2.9% of total number of transactions were mortgage" year="2005">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline in 2003 was estimated at 0.3%, but more accurate figures were found in 2005.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2005-12-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2012-02-29"></period-end>
     <target value="25% increase on baseline figure.">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The figure of 25% has been exceeded at times. Figure for 2011 is 24%.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="828% increase on the base line figure.">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">There were 36,495 in 2011. This equates to 24% of the total number of transactions that are mortgages. From 2.9% to 24% representsan 828% increase.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
